title: AWS v2 Glacier: Vault
agents: aws_v2
catalog: cloud/aws
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the archives of an AWS/Glacier vault and reports

 - the size of the vault

 - the number of archives

 - the tags of the vault

 To make this check work you have to configure the related
 special agent {Amazon Web Services (AWS) v2}.

 There are no default levels. Upper levels on the vault size
 are configurable via the rule "AWS v2/Glacier vault objects".

discovery:
 Each vault is a piggyback host with the name {<vault name>}.
 One service is created on this host.
